_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le15ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Past Tense and Past Continuous tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events that are   finished.</br> You use the Past Continuous to talk about events or an action that was happening at a time in the past."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I played baseball all through grade school. How about you?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I wasn't interested in sports much. I was always playing around on the computer."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Simple Past tense verbs can be regular or irregular.</br> Regular verbs end in <span class=\"italic\">-ed</span> or <span class=\"italic\">-ied</span>.</br> Irregular verbs change in different ways.</br> For questions in the past, you use the auxiliary <span class=\"italic\">did</span> followed by  the verb in the base form, like <span class=\"italic\">Did you ask\u2026?</span></br> <span class=\"italic\"> Did</span> is the past form of <span class=\"italic\">to do</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For Past Continuous, we add was/were + verb\u201cing\u201d to verbs.  Some verbs need a change to the last letter to add \u201cing\u201d."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"grow\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"grew\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were growing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"rent\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"rented\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were renting\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"play\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"played\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were playing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tell\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"told\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were telling\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"try\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tried\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were trying\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"see\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"saw\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"----------\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"attack\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"attacked\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were attacking\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to grow up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to gain in years from a child to an adult"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Peter and Sally both grew up in Boston. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about your personal past and history."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "grade school"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a term used more in the U.S. to refer to the years 